  {
   "heading": "### **base** R",
   "segment_index": "S7.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/dates.qmd:102-102",
   "tr_span": "chapters/dates.jp.qmd:94-94",
   "proposition": "English says that when dates are supplied as numbers you must give as.Date() the ORIGIN DATE; the Japanese says you must specify the FORMAT of the original date (元の日付の形式を指定します).",
   "reader_consequence": "A Japanese reader with Excel serial numbers looks for a strptime format string instead of the origin= argument, and their as.Date() call fails or returns wrong dates. The instruction also contradicts the same file's own Excel section (dates.jp.qmd:221, 231), which correctly says to pass the origin date to origin=.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "### **lubridate**",
   "segment_index": "S8.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/dates.qmd:150-150",
   "tr_span": "chapters/dates.jp.qmd:140-140",
   "proposition": "English says the lubridate helper FUNCTIONS are named after abbreviations of date formats; the Japanese instead attributes the abbreviation-derivation to the date SYNONYMS (日付フォーマットの略語に由来した日付の同義語), and never states that the function names encode the date-part order.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Japanese reader is not told that ymd/mdy/dmy are themselves the year-month-day abbreviations, so they must infer the naming rule from the examples and are more likely to pick the wrong helper for an unlisted order such as year-day-month.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "### Epiweek alternatives",
   "segment_index": "S26.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/dates.qmd:611-611",
   "tr_span": "chapters/dates.jp.qmd:585-585",
   "proposition": "English says tsibble::yearweek() is another alternative FOR time series; the Japanese says it is suitable INSTEAD OF time series (時系列の代わりに).",
   "reader_consequence": "A Japanese reader understands yearweek() as a replacement for time-series analysis rather than as a week-format helper intended for use inside time-series work, and may skip it when following the Time series and outbreak detection chapter that the same sentence points to.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  }
